</pre> panels(     {         "clusters": mf.DiffusionMaps().fit_transform(X_clust),     },     y_clust, ) <p>Each cluster collapses to roughly one point: the eigenvectors are near constant within a cluster. PHATE shows the same problem less aggressively, because the log and the MDS keep a little spread. With ten near-disconnected components the spectrum has about ten eigenvalues close to 1, and two dimensions can't separate them all, hence the clusters crowding the middle. Diffusion maps collapsing harder than PHATE on your data is a signal in itself: it is more cluster than manifold. Reach for t-SNE, UMAP or PaCMAP.</p> In [9]: Copied! <pre>panels(
